{"id": "EUVD-2026-102528", "enisaUuid": "9e39ea9e-e930-34c9-95fc-e1e4acaf8938", "description": "unarr through 1.1.1 contains an off-by-one heap-based buffer overflow in tar_get_name() in tar/parse-tar.c, reachable through the ar_entry_get_name() API. Attackers can supply a crafted TAR archive with a full ustar prefix and name to write a NUL byte past the allocation, corrupting heap memory and crashing the process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:39:08", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/unarr-tar-zip-oob", "https://github.com/selmf/unarr/blob/b211040df83dee513362cdeb9bd87afa26fd5e38/tar/parse-tar.c#L242-L254", "https://github.com/selmf/unarr", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/unarr-through-1.1.1-off-by-one-heap-buffer-overflow-via-tar-get-name"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2v49-qr2f-xxxp", "CVE-2026-111273"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f870a707-50bf-38e5-b1f1-0169ff684024", "product": {"name": "unarr", "vendor": {"name": "selmf"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.1.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bc603887-1d2f-34a3-af2e-42e29f08b250", "vendor": {"name": "selmf"}}], "isExploited": false}